  "step_by_step_reasoning": "The architecture shows an end-to-end data processing pipeline for ad events. Data enters via Kafka into Spark Streaming, which writes raw parquet data into an initial S3 bucket. Airflow triggers batch processing jobs on an EKS cluster (running Spark with Spotinst) which ingests raw data from S3, writes aggregated results to a secondary S3 bucket, and directly populates Cassandra. S3 aggregated data is read by Presto and EMR. EMR populates Druid. Finally, Cassandra, Presto, and Druid feed into a central Dashboard UI.",
